title: "Photo Share design"
status: draft
date: 2026-10-24
related: []
---

## Summary

Photo Share lets a family keep photos in albums and share an album by link.

## Goals, non-goals and success criteria

### Goals

A person uploads photos, groups them in albums and shares an album with a link.

### Non-goals

No editing of photos, because the brief asks for storage and sharing only.

### Success criteria

A page of 50 photos shows within two seconds on a phone.

## Context and constraints

The users are a family. They use phones. We assumed one language, English.

## The product at user level

A person signs in, makes an album and adds photos. A wrong link shows a page that says the album is gone.

## Decisions

- **Decided 2026-10-24:** An album link works until its owner turns it off.
  The brief does not say how long a link lives, and a family reopens old links.
  (Owner decisions: links-last)
- **Decided 2026-10-24:** Only the owner deletes photos.
  Guests only look.

## Open questions

- **q1:** May guests download photos?
  (Who can answer: The product owner)
- **q2:** How many photos may one album hold?
  (Who can answer: The product owner)
- **q3:** Is a second language needed?
  (Who can answer: The family)

## Notes

- The brief names no budget.
